{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>With this shall Aharon come into the holy place.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): 'with this' — with this arrangement, that is, with the ordering of the offerings and the deeds and the entire order of the Day of Atonements that he proceeds to arrange." "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> <b>בזאת</b> — the first Temple stood 410 years, corresponding to the numerical value of בזא״ת; 'he shall come' alludes to the duration of the future Temple's standing, which is near." "<b>And by way of the Kabbalah:</b> <b>בזאת</b> ('with this') is Knesset Yisra'el, and the witness to this is the language of <b>יבא</b> ('he shall come') — for from there it begins and ascends and comes into the holy place, which is the Ḥokhmah, and she is the source of blessing; and so it is written (Psalms 134:2): ״שאו ידיכם קדש וברכו את ה׳״. And from this the masters of truth said in the Midrash, and it is the explanation of this verse, 'with this shall Aharon come into the holy place' — when the High Priest entered the Holy of Holies he had in his hand bundles upon bundles of commandments: in the merit of the Torah, as it is said (Deuteronomy 4:44) ״וזאת התורה״; in the merit of circumcision, as it is said (Genesis 17:10) ״זאת בריתי אשר תשמרו״; in the merit of Shabbat, as it is said (Isaiah 56:2) ״אשרי אנוש יעשה זאת״; in the merit of Jerusalem, as it is said (Ezekiel 5:5) ״זאת ירושלים בתוך הגוים שמתיה״; in the merit of the tribes, as it is said (Genesis 49:28) ״וזאת אשר דבר להם אביהם״; in the merit of Yehudah, as it is said (Deuteronomy 33:7) ״וזאת ליהודה״; in the merit of Yisra'el, as it is said (Song of Songs 7:8) ״זאת קומתך דמתה לתמר״; in the merit of the terumah, as it is said (Exodus 25:3) ״וזאת התרומה״; in the merit of the tithes, as it is said (Malachi 3:10) ״ובחנוני נא בזאת״; in the merit of the offerings, as it is said: <b>בזאת יבא אהרן אל הקדש</b>. All these words allude to this measure (מדה), for they all share one matter and all go to one place — it is the tenth, holy; from there he comes into the holy place, and this is clear."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:25:53.103669575Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}